        "title": "A leaf is an organ made of tissues",
        "text": "Different tissues work together in a leaf. The epidermis forms a protective surface; the upper epidermis is usually transparent so light can reach photosynthetic tissue. Palisade mesophyll cells near the upper surface contain many chloroplasts and absorb light for photosynthesis. The cutaway separates layers to make them visible; real layers are closely joined.",
