        "title": "Air spaces shorten the gas route",
        "text": "Spongy mesophyll has irregularly arranged cells and intercellular air spaces. These spaces allow gases to move through the leaf towards and away from cells. Spongy cells can also photosynthesise. Stomata are pores in the epidermis; pairs of guard cells control their opening. Carbon dioxide enters for photosynthesis while oxygen and water vapour can leave.",
