        "title": "The vein links supply and removal",
        "text": "Xylem supplies water and mineral ions to the leaf. Phloem carries dissolved sugars from leaves to other plant parts for immediate use or storage. These transport tissues connect roots, stems and leaves. Leaf epidermis, mesophyll and transport tissues are parts of one organ; a leaf is not a single cell.",
