        "title": "Water moves by osmosis",
        "text": "When soil solution is more dilute than cell contents, water has a net movement into the root hair by osmosis through a partially permeable membrane. If the soil solution is sufficiently concentrated, net movement can reverse. Water molecules continue moving both ways; osmosis describes the net result. Water uptake itself is not a direct ATP-driven pump.",
        "scene": "plant:root:water"
